The class linker logs each class, method and field it fails to resolve (the Unity test APK probe, minato_resolve_log.h).

An app that catches a NoClassDefFoundError names no gap: Unity's activity died on a missing android.app.Dialog, and
the run showed only a later NoSuchFieldError. Where DoResolveType turns a ClassNotFoundException into a
NoClassDefFoundError, and where ResolveMethod, ResolveField and ResolveFieldJLS throw NoSuchMethodError and
NoSuchFieldError, a warning with the tag minato-resolve names what is missing and the method that asks, once; the
verifier names the method it verifies for the resolutions it makes.

